Guard NimBLEAdvertisedDevice::findAdvField() against a corrupt/oversized
m_payload.

On BLE_GAP_EVENT_DISC_COMPLETE during active scanning, NimBLEScan flushes its
"waiting list" (connectable + scannable peers that never returned a scan
response within the window) by calling onResult() on each device. If such a
device's m_payload is stale/corrupt, the field walk in findAdvField() runs off
the end of the buffer — observed on the JC4880P443C as a Load access fault at
PSRAM_top+4 (0x4c000004), rebooting the board once per scan cycle (~every 5 s).
The crash surfaced when an OpenAir PLUS A/C (connectable, slow/absent scan
response) was in range of the supervisor scan.

The supervisor scan is now passive (main/victronble.cpp), which avoids the
waiting list entirely; this guard is defense-in-depth that also protects the
user-initiated active discovery scans. Applied by scripts/apply_patches.py.

--- a/managed_components/h2zero__esp-nimble-cpp/src/NimBLEAdvertisedDevice.cpp
+++ b/managed_components/h2zero__esp-nimble-cpp/src/NimBLEAdvertisedDevice.cpp
@@ uint8_t NimBLEAdvertisedDevice::findAdvField(uint8_t type, uint8_t index, size_t* data_loc) const {
     size_t  length = m_payload.size();
+    // TruMinus guard: a corrupt/oversized payload (seen on the active-scan
+    // DISC_COMPLETE waiting-list flush) would make the walk below run off the
+    // end of the buffer (load fault past the PSRAM top).  62 B = max legacy
+    // adv+scanrsp, 1650 B = max BLE5 extended adv; anything larger is
+    // corruption, so bail.
+    if (length > 1650) {
+        return 0;
+    }
     size_t  data   = 0;
     uint8_t count  = 0;
